I remember a list of intrinsic abilities was posted to this forum a couple of
months ago.  I think the samurai had gained powers of speed and stealth at
later levels.  If someone has a copy, then could you please confirm this.

Personally, I have the best games with either the smaurai or the magic-user.

Would it also be possible to consider making spells remain in memory
permanently, or to only forget them if they are totally abused (ie casted
once a turn for 5 turns).  If this is too powerful, slow down the regeneration
of power points.

I feel this way, the magic-user would then be able to use magic.  Not requiring
to find Stormbinger to do some real damage, but instead using fireballs etc.
as is more becoming to a magic-user.  Meanwhile a barbarian, given little power
and a slow regeneration might be able to show off to his friends by casting
the odd magic missile.

I have played Larn, in which spells can be severely abused, but since Hack
requires some spells to drain spell power faster than others I can't see this
as much of a problem.  It seems to work fairly well in Moria.


